 "description": "What is this Base address? One call returns whether it has bytecode and how much, ERC-165 answers for ERC721 and ERC1155, ERC20 metadata, EIP-1967 implementation and beacon slots, and EIP-1167 minimal proxy detection. Replaces about six calls. States in the payload that the classification is best-effort: a contract can answer ERC-165 dishonestly and a proxy can delegate anywhere. Pay 8000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
